abstract: >-
  A 32-bit, 6-stage pipelined Von Neumann RISC processor (IF -> ID -> EX1 ->
  EX2 -> MEM -> WB) designed in pure single-edge synthesizable VHDL-2008 by
  Anton Magdy (@AntonMagdy111), featuring a custom 26-instruction ISA, unified
  4096 x 32-bit memory, strictly age-ordered forwarding with zero-stall WB->MEM
  store/output bypass, 16-entry 2-bit saturating BTB, 4-deep CCR shadow stack,
  14 always-on assertions, SVA/covergroup companion, C++17 two-pass assembler,
  and constrained-random RTL vs. Golden-ISS cosimulation suite.
